Title: Git and PR Rules
Status: CANONICAL

- Branch regex (SER-96): `^(feature|bugfix|chore)/SER-[1-9][0-9]*-[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$`. Use Spanish Conventional Commits.
- Prefer human-chosen `chore/SER-*` / `feature/SER-*` / `bugfix/SER-*` branches; do not treat Linear auto branches or `cursor/*` as canonical work branches for governance tickets.
- No force-push to shared branches; do not push directly to `main`.
- PR body machine headings (exact): Linear, Requirements, Architecture, Use cases, Contracts, Design, Tests, Docs / Runbooks, Security / Data impact, Migrations.
- Linear section: `Primary: SER-N` then optional `Related: SER-N, SER-M`.
- No AI/tool/coauthor/generated-by attribution in contribution metadata (branch/title/commit/PR trailers).
- AUTO_MERGE=OFF; merge only after explicit human approval.
